## Three things you should rule on

1. **Item 9 date.** This doc has no date field. It records `Observed exit code:` lines and no capture date, so there was nothing to set to 2026-10-26 and I added no new date line. Say the word if you want one appended.
2. **Item 9 em dash.** The clean-run console line is `OK` plus an em dash plus `0 broken markdown links.` Your brief bans writing an em dash, so that one line is omitted from both clean blocks. Everything else in those blocks is verbatim, and the framing sentence at line 52 now states the tree is link-clean with an empty broken set. Restoring full verbatim output means accepting that one em dash.
3. **Item 8 rewrap.** The mandated prefix makes line 486 102 characters against neighbours of 82, so it is longer than them either way. No rewrap can shorten it and no word moved across the break, so lines 487-488 stay as they were.

Also worth knowing: the deletion of the six pre-existing broken links made two other lines in item 9 unstale-able. Line 52's "six pre-existing broken links survive, so the baseline is exit 1" and the `[plus the same six pre-existing broken links ...]` line in the injected block both asserted a non-clean tree, so both changed. That is beyond the literal line range and inside the file the brief named.

Adjacent, untouched, out of scope: `manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/ac-coverage-single-source-ratio.md:85` still reads `16 passed, 0 failed`, an unrelated coverage figure.

